The displayed simply-laced tree has arms of lengths $2$, $1$, and $3$ from its trivalent vertex, so it is the finite <E7 Coxeter group>[type $E_7$ Coxeter graph]. Its Gram matrix is the $E_7$ Cartan matrix, which has positive leading principal minors in a leaf-removal ordering and determinant $2$. By <Sylvester's criterion> it is positive definite. It is therefore positive semidefinite and nondegenerate as well: the three answers are yes, yes, and yes.

